<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Managua</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Managua is the capital and largest city of Nicaragua, on the southern shore of Lake Managua. A small town between the rival cities of León and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada">Granada</a>, it was chosen as the capital in 1852 as a compromise. It was devastated by earthquakes in 1931 and 1972, the second killing about 10,000 people, and its old centre was never fully rebuilt.</p></div>
